method.description:
Collects writes inside [param body] and commits them as one batch.
[param body] receives a [NetwTransaction] and calls [method NetwTransaction.queue_upsert] for each record to write. The commit runs once [param body] returns, which is what makes it happen exactly once however the body exits.
The promise resolves with an [enum @GlobalScope.Error]. Read the code from [member NetwPromise.result]. [signal transaction_committed] is emitted only after a commit returns [constant @GlobalScope.OK].
[codeblock]
var err: Error = await db.transaction(
    func(tx: NetwTransaction) -> void:
        tx.queue_upsert(&"rocks", &"rock_1", {&"health": 50})
).wait()
[/codeblock]
A caller that must not suspend, such as a pump that would let its next round start inside this one, chains [method NetwPromise.then] on the same result instead of awaiting it.
